    <edge source="proxy:OEB-H01" target="indicator:OEB">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">OEB-H01</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">linear</data>
      <data key="d28">r = 0.5-0.7 in NOx-limited regions</data>
      <data key="d29">NO₂ is a primary precursor to ozone formation through photochemical reactions. In NOx-limited regimes (most rural areas and KBAs), increased NO₂ availability directly increases ozone formation rates.</data>
      <data key="d30">inconclusive</data>
      <data key="d31" />
      <data key="d32" />
      <data key="d33" />
      <data key="d34" />
      <data key="d35" />
      <data key="d36" />
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["Data source substitution: Hypothesis specifies 'CAMS Global Reanalysis tropospheric NO\u2082 column density' but script failed to acquire this and attempted World Bank indicators (EN.ATM.NO2.PC, EN.ATM.NOX.KT.CE, EN.CLC.NOXD.MT). The script documents this as a fallback due to API limitations, but notes indicate none of these World Bank proxies returned sufficient data.", "Proxy variable mismatch: The attempted World Bank substitutes are NOx emissions (kt CO\u2082-equiv) and per-capita NO\u2082 concentration \u2014 these are materially different from satellite-derived tropospheric NO\u2082 column density (molecules/cm\u00b2). Column density measures atmospheric vertical integration; emissions are ground-level sources; per-capita concentration is a population-weighted average. The mechanism depends on column density specifically.", "No verification actually performed: The script exits early with 'inconclusive' verdict because proxy data acquisition failed (result.json shows n_observations=0, n_countries=0). No correlation, partial correlation, or functional form testing was conducted. The inconclusive verdict is appropriate but masks the underlying data authenticity issue.", "Data source not documented as substitution: While data_quality_notes mentions the failed fallback attempts, the script did not proceed to test with a documented alternative. The verification was abandoned rather than executed with a clearly-noted proxy substitution."]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:OEB-H01" target="source:copernicus_atmosphere_monitoring_service">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:OEB-H02" target="indicator:OEB">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">OEB-H02</data>
      <data key="d26">negative</data>
      <data key="d27">log-linear</data>
      <data key="d28">r = -0.5 to -0.7</data>
      <data key="d29">Lower PBL height suppresses vertical mixing, concentrating ozone and precursors near the surface. Shallow mixing heights are explicitly linked to ozone accumulation in boundary layers.</data>
      <data key="d30">inconclusive</data>
      <data key="d31" />
      <data key="d32" />
      <data key="d33" />
      <data key="d34" />
      <data key="d35" />
      <data key="d36" />
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["CRITICAL: Hypothesis specifies ERA5 PBL height as data source; verification agent could not access ERA5 and reported 'inconclusive' verdict without testing any proxy variable.", "CRITICAL: Agent attempted to use surface temperature (EN.ATM.TEMP.K) as PBL proxy but then failed to actually load and test this data, ultimately reporting n_observations=0 and no statistical test performed.", "MAJOR: The proxy variable tested (if temperature had been loaded) would be materially different from the hypothesis's specified variable (PBL height). Surface temperature and PBL height are distinct meteorological variables with opposite causal relationships to ozone in many contexts.", "MAJOR: Data source authenticity compromised\u2014hypothesis specifies ERA5/ECMWF, but agent attempted World Bank climate indicators and NCEP data, neither of which are equivalent to planetary boundary layer height from reanalysis.", "PROCESS: Agent's extensive troubleshooting and honest reporting of data unavailability is commendable, but the result is an inconclusive verdict with zero observations, making it impossible to evaluate hypothesis validity.", "Documentation issue: The data_quality_notes correctly explain why ERA5 was inaccessible but do not document any actual proxy substitution that was tested (because none was successfully loaded)."]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:OEB-H02" target="source:ecmwf/copernicus">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:OEB-H03" target="indicator:OEB">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">OEB-H03</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">linear</data>
      <data key="d28">r = 0.6-0.8 for NO₂, r = 0.5-0.7 for PM₂.₅</data>
      <data key="d29">NO₂ and PM₂.₅ share common emission sources with ozone precursors and co-occur in photochemical smog episodes. NO₂ is directly involved in ozone formation chemistry.</data>
      <data key="d30">confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">0.3046753579384338</data>
      <data key="d40">2.1993809482527447e-74</data>
      <data key="d41">0.18277064920549402</data>
      <data key="d42">3420</data>
      <data key="d43">0.5013144339937928</data>
      <data key="d36">quadratic</data>
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["hypothesis_interpretation: Hypothesis specified 'Ground-based NO\u2082 and PM\u2082.\u2085 Concentrations from air quality monitoring stations,' but the agent substituted World Bank PM\u2082.\u2085 mean annual exposure (EN.ATM.PM25.MC.M3), which is a spatially-averaged exposure metric, not ground-based station concentrations. NO\u2082 was not obtained at all.", "data_source_authentic: Hypothesis cites WAQI (https://waqi.info) as the data source; agent failed to access WAQI and instead used World Bank PM\u2082.\u2085 without adequately documenting this as a material substitution. The data_quality_notes mention the substitution but do not flag it as a departure from the hypothesis specification.", "bivariate_correlation_weak: Pearson r=0.305 is substantially below the hypothesis's predicted range of 0.5\u20130.8 for PM\u2082.\u2085, suggesting either weak proxy alignment or a genuine failure of the hypothesis.", "spearman_much_lower: Spearman rho=0.183 vs Pearson r=0.305 indicates the relationship is non-linear or driven by outliers; the quadratic form (R\u00b2=0.109) barely improves on linear (R\u00b2=0.093), raising questions about functional form validity.", "partial_correlation_paradox: Partial r=0.501 (controlling for log GDP) is substantially higher than raw Pearson r=0.305, suggesting GDP confounds the raw relationship\u2014a red flag that the raw proxy-target link may be spurious or heavily mediated by economic factors not in the hypothesis mechanism."]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:OEB-H03" target="source:waqi">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
