    <edge source="proxy:OEB-H09" target="indicator:SDA">
      <data key="d23">inferred_candidate</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d44">cross_indicator_transfer</data>
      <data key="d45">0.8</data>
      <data key="d46">Proxy OEB-H09 confirmed/partially confirmed for sibling indicator; untested for SDA</data>
      <data key="d47">["OEB-H09"]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:OEB-H10" target="indicator:OEB">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">OEB-H10</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">linear</data>
      <data key="d28">r = 0.2-0.4</data>
      <data key="d29">Ammonia emissions react with NOx to form compounds participating in ozone formation chemistry. Livestock systems contribute reactive nitrogen availability that drives ozone formation.</data>
      <data key="d30">partially_confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">0.060394575251958</data>
      <data key="d40">0.00021264211267465837</data>
      <data key="d41">0.07012348618277692</data>
      <data key="d42">3756</data>
      <data key="d43">0.01967113569472007</data>
      <data key="d36">quadratic</data>
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["MAJOR: Hypothesis specifies 'Ammonia Emissions and Livestock Density' from EDGAR (0.1\u00b0 \u00d7 0.1\u00b0 gridded data), but script used World Bank's 'Livestock production index' (AG.PRD.LVSK.XD) \u2014 a fundamentally different variable (economic production vs. physical emissions/density).", "MAJOR: Primary data source not authentic. Hypothesis requires EDGAR NetCDF gridded emissions inventory; script substituted World Bank macro-indicator. While documented in data_quality_notes, this is a material deviation from the specified source.", "MODERATE: Correlation is extremely weak (r=0.060, p&lt;0.001 for Pearson; rho=0.070 for Spearman) and disappears when controlling for GDP per capita (partial r=0.020, p=0.236), suggesting confounding by economic development rather than a causal ammonia-ozone mechanism.", "MODERATE: The hypothesis specifies the mechanism operates on 'ozone formation chemistry' where ammonia reacts with NOx, but a livestock production index does not directly capture ammonia flux or the reactive nitrogen availability that drives this chemistry.", "MINOR: The verdict is 'partially_confirmed' despite the partial correlation becoming non-significant (p=0.236) when controlling for log(GPC), which weakens the evidence substantially."]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:OEB-H10" target="source:ec_joint_research_centre">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
