    <edge source="proxy:PHL-H07" target="indicator:PHL">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">PHL-H07</data>
      <data key="d26">negative</data>
      <data key="d27">log-linear</data>
      <data key="d28">strong (estimated)</data>
      <data key="d29">Nighttime lights are the gold standard proxy for human settlement and infrastructure. If a protected area is truly undisturbed, nighttime light radiance should be near zero. Increases indicate construction of buildings, facilities, and roads</data>
      <data key="d30">partially_confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">-0.14901245796395493</data>
      <data key="d40">0.0497145314436631</data>
      <data key="d41">-0.12651894811476025</data>
      <data key="d42">174</data>
      <data key="d35" />
      <data key="d36">linear</data>
      <data key="d48">5</data>
      <data key="d38">["CRITICAL: Proxy variable is materially different from hypothesis specification. Hypothesis targets VIIRS Nighttime Lights specifically within protected area boundaries (a spatially constrained, within-PA geospatial signal). Verification script uses World Bank 'Access to electricity (%)' (EG.ELC.ACCS.ZS), which is a national-level aggregate measure unrelated to PA boundaries.", "CRITICAL: Year alignment issue. Target (PHL) is 2022; proxy (EG.ELC.ACCS.ZS) years are not specified in output, but the script merges on 'iso' only when years don't overlap, creating temporal mismatch. The data_quality_notes confirm 'Proxy year does not exactly match target year; merged on ISO code only.'", "Data source not authentic. Hypothesis specifies 'VIIRS Day/Night Band Nighttime Lights' from 'Earth Observation Group (EOG)' as the data source. Script explicitly documents that 'Direct VIIRS Nighttime Lights in Protected Areas data were not available' and substituted World Bank electricity data instead. This substitution was not pre-documented in the hypothesis and represents a fundamental pivot away from the specified proxy.", "Mechanistic validity compromised. The causal link between national-level electricity access and integrity of protected areas (no buildings/cropland within PA boundaries) is weak and indirect. Electricity access measures a country-level development indicator; in-PA nighttime lights would measure PA-specific human disturbance. The substitute operates at a different geographic scale.", "Partial correlation not computed. Script states 'Partial r = null' in result, limiting the ability to control for confounders (e.g., GPC). This weakens the causal interpretation."]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:PHL-H07" target="source:earth_observation_group_(eog)">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:PHL-H07" target="indicator:PAE">
      <data key="d23">inferred_candidate</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d44">cross_indicator_transfer</data>
      <data key="d45">0.8</data>
      <data key="d46">Proxy PHL-H07 confirmed/partially confirmed for sibling indicator; untested for PAE</data>
      <data key="d47">["PHL-H07"]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:PHL-H08" target="indicator:PHL">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">PHL-H08</data>
      <data key="d26">negative</data>
      <data key="d27">linear</data>
      <data key="d28">very strong (estimated)</data>
      <data key="d29">In forested biomes, croplands and buildings cannot be established without first removing the canopy. Tree cover loss is the absolute prerequisite to human encroachment, with vast majority of deforestation in tropical PAs being anthropogenic and driven by agricultural expansion</data>
      <data key="d30">partially_confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">0.23836377478967233</data>
      <data key="d40">0.0015383368719262213</data>
      <data key="d41">0.27513653577835356</data>
      <data key="d42">174</data>
      <data key="d35" />
      <data key="d36" />
      <data key="d48">4</data>
      <data key="d38">["CRITICAL: Proxy variable is fundamentally different from hypothesis specification. Hypothesis requires 'tree cover loss' (a rate/change metric in protected areas), but agent used 'forest area' (a stock metric, global, not PA-specific). These are conceptually distinct variables.", "CRITICAL: Year alignment problem. Proxy uses 'most recent available year per country' (likely 2020-2021) while target is year 2022. Cross-sectional merge on ISO only ignores temporal dimension entirely. Proxy year varies by country but is not aligned to target year.", "CRITICAL: Data source not authentic. Hypothesis specifies Hansen Global Forest Change dataset (satellite raster at 30m resolution, requires GIS overlay with WDPA boundaries). Agent used World Bank tabular forest area indicator (AG.LND.FRST.ZS), which is a different data source with different methodology, not a reasonable substitution but a fundamental substitution.", "Direction inversion: Hypothesis expects negative correlation (more tree loss \u2192 more encroachment). Agent reversed this to positive (more forest area \u2192 higher PHL score), then declared 'partially_confirmed' despite this direction flip. The verdict does not align with the original hypothesis direction.", "Missing spatial specificity: Hypothesis explicitly targets 'protected areas in forested biomes.' Proxy is global forest area, not PA-specific, losing critical geographic scope.", "No functional form or partial correlation results: Script attempted these analyses but did not include results in JSON output, limiting verification depth.", "Data quality notes acknowledge the substitution but still yield 'partially_confirmed' verdict\u2014this is inconsistent. A materially different proxy should typically warrant 'inconclusive' or 'unconfirmed' rather than 'partially_confirmed'."]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:PHL-H08" target="source:university_of_maryland_/_global_forest_watch">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:PHL-H08" target="indicator:PAE">
      <data key="d23">inferred_candidate</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d44">cross_indicator_transfer</data>
      <data key="d45">0.8</data>
      <data key="d46">Proxy PHL-H08 confirmed/partially confirmed for sibling indicator; untested for PAE</data>
      <data key="d47">["PHL-H08"]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:PHL-H09" target="indicator:PHL">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">PHL-H09</data>
      <data key="d26">negative</data>
      <data key="d27">threshold</data>
      <data key="d28">moderate (estimated)</data>
      <data key="d29">If a country has rapidly growing fertilizer imports but stagnant official arable land, it indicates aggressive agricultural intensification. In countries with high land scarcity, this pressure forces farmers to expand into protected areas</data>
      <data key="d30">rejected</data>
      <data key="d39">0.07616136625355374</data>
      <data key="d40">0.31786840935366406</data>
      <data key="d41">0.021147526979697597</data>
      <data key="d42">174</data>
      <data key="d35" />
      <data key="d36">log-linear</data>
      <data key="d48">6</data>
      <data key="d38">["YEAR ALIGNMENT CRITICAL: Proxy data (fertilizer kg/ha) from 2019\u20132022 most-recent-year-per-country is merged against PHL target data from 2022 only, matching on ISO code without enforcing temporal alignment. For ~93% of the 174 countries, the fertilizer observation is from a different year than 2022, yet treated as contemporaneous. This violates proxy-target temporal alignment.", "HYPOTHESIS INTERPRETATION MISMATCH: Hypothesis specifies 'synthetic fertilizer consumption divided by officially recognized arable land OUTSIDE OF PROTECTED AREAS.' The World Bank AG.CON.FERT.ZS indicator is fertilizer per hectare of ALL arable land (no subtraction of protected areas). The script acknowledges this limitation in data_quality_notes but does not flag it as a material divergence from hypothesis specification.", "DATA SOURCE SUBSTITUTION NOT DOCUMENTED: Hypothesis specifies FAOSTAT as data source; script uses World Bank AG.CON.FERT.ZS instead. While a reasonable proxy substitution, this is not the source specified in the hypothesis, and the shift from FAOSTAT to World Bank is not explicitly documented as a source change in result.json or marked in data_quality_notes as a substitution decision.", "PARTIAL CORRELATION FAILED WITHOUT ROBUST FALLBACK: Partial correlation (controlling for GDP per capita) could not be computed due to numerical issues in pingouin. Script accepts this failure gracefully but does not attempt alternative methods (e.g., manual OLS residualization or robust regression). This weakens causal interpretation.", "POTENTIAL OUTLIER INFLUENCE NOT ASSESSED: Script performs no outlier detection, leverage analysis, or sensitivity testing. With 174 countries and R\u00b2 values &lt; 0.009, the correlation is extremely weak; script does not investigate whether a few high-fertilizer or extreme-PHL countries are driving the null result.", "WEAK EFFECT STRENGTH NOT CONTEXTUALIZED: Pearson r=0.076 (p=0.318) and Spearman rho=0.021 (p=0.782) are both non-significant and negligible. The verdict is 'rejected,' which is appropriate, but the script does not discuss whether the hypothesis mechanism might operate only in a subset (high land scarcity countries per hypothesis subpopulation definition) rather than globally."]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:PHL-H09" target="source:food_and_agriculture_organization_of_the_un">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:SPI-H01" target="indicator:SPI">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">SPI-H01</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">linear</data>
      <data key="d28">strong (direct conceptual alignment)</data>
      <data key="d29">PARC and SPI both measure representativeness rather than area alone. Countries achieving high PARC scores across priority ecosystem types simultaneously achieve higher SPI values for endemic species concentrated in those ecosystem types.</data>
      <data key="d30">confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">0.35143071175568363</data>
      <data key="d40">2.3130141215448735e-50</data>
      <data key="d41">0.4407063530994446</data>
      <data key="d42">1692</data>
      <data key="d43">0.2998263842488209</data>
      <data key="d36">quadratic</data>
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["CRITICAL: The proxy variable is materially different from the hypothesis. PARC measures representativeness and connectivity of protected area networks across ecosystem types; ER.MRN.PTMR.ZS measures only marine PA coverage as a percentage. These are conceptually distinct\u2014coverage \u2260 representativeness.", "CRITICAL: Data source mismatch. The hypothesis specifies PARC from GEO BON/IPBES; the script used World Bank marine PA data (ER.MRN.PTMR.ZS). The substitution was documented in data_quality_notes but represents a fundamental proxy swap, not a reasonable substitute.", "The script's own data_quality_notes acknowledge this is an 'exploratory substitution' and that the proxy 'measures protected area coverage...rather than representativeness per se.' This admission of conceptual divergence should have triggered a hypothesis_interpretation_ok=false flag.", "The mechanistic explanation provided in the hypothesis explicitly references 'representativeness and connectivity components' and 'endemic species concentrated in [priority] ecosystem types.' Marine PA coverage cannot test these mechanisms.", "The result verdict is 'confirmed' based on a proxy that does not test the actual hypothesis. A positive correlation with marine PA coverage does not validate a hypothesis about representativeness indices."]</data>
    </edge>
