    <edge source="proxy:SPI-H05" target="indicator:SPI">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">SPI-H05</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">log-linear</data>
      <data key="d28">moderate with substantial scatter</data>
      <data key="d29">Initial increases in protected area percentage yield large SPI gains as protected areas capture unprotected habitat hotspots. Beyond approximately 20-30% land protection, additional gains diminish as remaining suitable habitat becomes marginal.</data>
      <data key="d30">confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">0.6039432416668155</data>
      <data key="d40">2.417247128523255e-211</data>
      <data key="d41">0.6318904160043814</data>
      <data key="d42">2124</data>
      <data key="d43">0.5987501019542326</data>
      <data key="d36">quadratic</data>
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["Functional form mismatch: hypothesis specifies log-linear, but result shows quadratic as best fit. Log-linear R\u00b2=null due to zero values in proxy data (countries with 0% protected area). This is a material discrepancy between predicted and observed functional form.", "The quadratic form is not mentioned in the hypothesis mechanism, which explicitly expects diminishing returns (log-linear behavior). A quadratic fit suggests the relationship may have a maximum and then decline, which is conceptually different from the monotonic diminishing-returns mechanism stated.", "Data coverage note: log-linear fit failure due to zero/low proxy values is acknowledged in data_quality_notes but creates uncertainty about whether the true functional form can be tested as hypothesized."]</data>
    </edge>
