    <edge source="proxy:SPI-H08" target="indicator:SPI">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">SPI-H08</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">threshold</data>
      <data key="d28">r=0.65-0.85 (estimated)</data>
      <data key="d29">Countries with large intact habitat patches can protect representative species assemblages efficiently, while countries where remaining habitat occurs in fragmented patches require disproportionate protected area expansion to achieve equivalent SPI. Large habitat patches enable strategic protected area placement for high SPI achievement.</data>
      <data key="d30">partially_confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">0.1575627504161815</data>
      <data key="d40">4.60638108755843e-34</data>
      <data key="d41">0.16835701433399838</data>
      <data key="d42">5892</data>
      <data key="d43">0.15911212686346393</data>
      <data key="d36">quadratic</data>
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["Proxy substitution changes hypothesis materially: 'Area of Habitat Remaining within Fragmented Landscape Patches' (requires geospatial fragmentation metrics) was replaced with 'Forest area (% of land area)' (a simple landscape coverage metric). Fragmentation geometry is the core mechanism; forest area % is a proxy for habitat availability only.", "Data source not authentic: hypothesis specifies Global Forest Watch and ESA CCI raster data; script uses World Bank forest area indicator instead. While documented in data_quality_notes, this is a fundamental substitution, not a reasonable approximation.", "Weak correlation (r=0.158) may reflect the poor fit between proxy and hypothesis. If fragmentation were central to the mechanism, a non-fragmentation proxy would be expected to show weaker or no relationship.", "The script acknowledges the substitution is 'imperfect' but proceeds with full statistical testing and a 'partially_confirmed' verdict. This overstates confidence given the conceptual mismatch."]</data>
    </edge>
