    <edge source="proxy:SPI-H09" target="indicator:SPI">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">SPI-H09</data>
      <data key="d26">negative</data>
      <data key="d27">linear</data>
      <data key="d28">r=-0.55 to -0.70 (estimated)</data>
      <data key="d29">Heavy chemical use in agricultural regions creates water quality and soil degradation impacts that penetrate into protected areas through groundwater and surface water flows. Protected areas within agricultural catchments experience eutrophication and chemical pollution that directly reduce aquatic species richness and abundance.</data>
      <data key="d30">rejected</data>
      <data key="d39">0.04855050533764781</data>
      <data key="d40">0.5210520403335829</data>
      <data key="d41">0.07072709409071037</data>
      <data key="d42">177</data>
      <data key="d43">-0.00843721458697423</data>
      <data key="d36">linear</data>
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["hypothesis_interpretation_ok: The hypothesis specifies 'Pesticide and Fertilizer Application Intensity' as the proxy, with explicit emphasis on pesticide use. The script uses only fertilizer consumption (AG.CON.FERT.ZS) as the primary proxy after pesticide data (AG.CON.PEST.ZS) returned empty. This is a material substitution\u2014pesticides and fertilizers have different chemical toxicity profiles and environmental pathways, and the hypothesis mechanism specifically emphasizes 'heavy pesticide use' and 'chemical pollution.' Using fertilizer alone does not adequately represent the proxy variable as described.", "data_source_authentic: The hypothesis specifies FAO pesticide statistics (https://www.worldometers.info/food-agriculture/pesticides-by-country/) as the data source. The script attempts World Bank indicators (AG.CON.FERT.ZS and AG.CON.PEST.ZS) instead. While these are FAO-sourced data delivered through World Bank, the specific Worldometers source was not accessed, and the substitution to fertilizer-only was not explicitly documented in data_quality_notes as a necessary adaptation (it is mentioned, but framed as a fallback rather than a documented limitation of accessing the original source).", "year_alignment_ok: The script uses cross-sectional analysis (most recent year per country) but matches GPC via 'nearest available year' rather than exact year match. For cross-sectional analysis, this nearest-year join is reasonable, but it introduces temporal slippage. The script does not clearly flag this as a potential source of error in causal inference, particularly when the nearest year may be several years apart.", "country_coverage_adequate: While n=177 countries appears adequate, the cross-sectional design (most recent year per country) collapses temporal variation and may mask important dynamics. The script switches between full panel (n=177) and cross-sectional designs without clear justification for the 30-observation threshold chosen."]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:SPI-H09" target="source:fao,_worldometer">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:SPI-H10" target="indicator:SPI">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">SPI-H10</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">linear</data>
      <data key="d28">r&gt;0.75 (estimated)</data>
      <data key="d29">eDNA sampling generates direct measure of species presence, absence, and community composition change over time. Protected areas with high species diversity detected through eDNA sampling, combined with stable or improving detection, indicate effective species protection and should correlate strongly with SPI habitat representativeness measures.</data>
      <data key="d30">partially_confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">0.1575627504161815</data>
      <data key="d40">4.60638108755843e-34</data>
      <data key="d41">0.16835701433399838</data>
      <data key="d42">5892</data>
      <data key="d43">0.15911212686346393</data>
      <data key="d36">quadratic</data>
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["CRITICAL: hypothesis_interpretation_ok = false. The hypothesis specifies 'Environmental DNA (eDNA) Detection Diversity' as the proxy variable\u2014a direct biodiversity observation metric. The script substituted 'Forest area (% of land area)' (AG.LND.FRST.ZS), which is a habitat structural measure, not species diversity detection. This is a materially different variable. Forest cover is a land-use proxy, not a measure of detected species community composition.", "CRITICAL: data_source_authentic = false. The hypothesis specifies the data source as 'Conservation Genetics Labs eDNA programs' from 'U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service, various research institutions.' The script did not fetch from this source (acknowledged as unavailable at country level) and instead used World Bank forest area data without explicitly documenting this as an unauthenticated substitution in the mechanistic narrative. The proxy_substitution field notes it is 'approximate' but the verification_method is 'exploratory_test' (not 'pending_data'), implying a test was completed on fundamentally different data.", "The correlation result (r=0.158, p&lt;0.001, n=5892) is statistically significant but weak, and the verdict 'partially_confirmed' is misleading given that the tested variable (forest cover) is conceptually distant from the hypothesis (eDNA species detection diversity).", "The script correctly notes that eDNA data is unavailable at country scale and coverage is &lt;5% of countries, but then proceeds to test a different hypothesis without clearly bifurcating the verdict: the hypothesis as specified is 'inconclusive due to data unavailability,' while the forest-area proxy test is a separate exploratory exercise.", "Country coverage (177 countries, 5892 observations) is adequate, but those observations are for forest cover, not eDNA diversity. The merge is temporally aligned (iso \u00d7 year), but the proxy variable is fundamentally misaligned with the hypothesis target.", "The verdict should be 'inconclusive' (due to data unavailability of the specified proxy), not 'partially_confirmed' (which implies the eDNA hypothesis was tested). The agent conflated 'we found a weak correlation with a different variable' with 'the hypothesis is supported.'"]</data>
    </edge>
