    <edge source="proxy:SPI-H11" target="indicator:SPI">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">SPI-H11</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">linear</data>
      <data key="d28">r=0.55-0.70 (estimated)</data>
      <data key="d29">Species with transnational migration routes must traverse protected area systems in origin and destination countries plus intermediate regions. Stable or increasing populations indicate that protected area networks provide meaningful habitat representation across entire geographic ranges, while declining populations suggest inadequate protection in critical bottleneck regions.</data>
