    <edge source="proxy:UWD-H01" target="indicator:UWD">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">UWD-H01</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">log-linear</data>
      <data key="d28">r ≈ 0.60–0.75</data>
      <data key="d29">Poor water plus weak sanitation leads to fecal-oral contamination and gastrointestinal disease, with countries having very poor water safety clustering at high diarrhea rates</data>
      <data key="d30">partially_confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">0.9111405166879349</data>
      <data key="d40">0.0</data>
      <data key="d41">0.946994230834955</data>
      <data key="d42">6176</data>
      <data key="d35" />
      <data key="d36">quadratic</data>
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["CRITICAL: Proxy variable substitution \u2014 hypothesis specifies 'Diarrheal disease notification rates' but actual proxy used is 'SH.DYN.MORT' (Under-5 mortality rate), a fundamentally different variable. Under-5 mortality has many causes (malaria, pneumonia, malnutrition, etc.) beyond diarrheal disease.", "CRITICAL: Data source mismatch \u2014 hypothesis specifies WHO GHO as source; script fell back to World Bank after WHO GHO API calls failed. Substitution is documented in data_quality_notes but represents a materially different source with different methodology.", "CRITICAL: Extraordinarily high correlation (r=0.911, rho=0.947) with p\u22480.0 across 6,176 observations from 193 countries is implausibly strong for an indirect proxy. Under-5 mortality is confounded by multiple competing causes; a near-perfect correlation suggests the proxy is measuring something different from the hypothesis mechanism.", "MAJOR: Functional form mismatch \u2014 hypothesis predicts log-linear relationship; script found quadratic (R\u00b2=0.8316 vs 0.5665 for log-linear), suggesting the mechanism is not log-linear as claimed.", "MAJOR: Partial correlation not computed (null in result) \u2014 GPC (GDP per capita) control could not be run, leaving economic confounding unaddressed. This is critical because Under-5 mortality is strongly driven by national wealth, as is water access.", "CONCERN: Outlier influence likely \u2014 with near-perfect correlation across 193 countries, the relationship may be driven by a few countries with extreme values rather than the causal mechanism described in the hypothesis.", "DATA QUALITY: Script documents data_quality_notes that proxy is 'related WASH/water-disease metric' but actual proxy (Under-5 mortality) is not specifically a water-disease metric \u2014 it conflates diarrhea with other leading causes of child death."]</data>
    </edge>
