    <edge source="proxy:UWD-H04" target="indicator:UWD">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">UWD-H04</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">nonlinear</data>
      <data key="d28">r ≈ 0.55–0.70</data>
      <data key="d29">HAV epidemiology mirrors WASH coverage: High-HDI countries have low prevalence &amp; older age at first infection; Low-HDI countries have early childhood infection via waterborne route</data>
      <data key="d30">partially_confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">0.07240011166192248</data>
      <data key="d40">2.6266229391194686e-07</data>
      <data key="d41">0.20125272056036017</data>
      <data key="d42">5046</data>
      <data key="d35" />
      <data key="d36" />
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["CRITICAL: Proxy variable mismatch. Hypothesis specifies 'reported acute hepatitis A cases per 100,000' or 'age-standardized seroprevalence (% with anti-HAV antibodies)'. Script used WHO GHO WHS3_41, which the data_quality_notes itself flags as 'may reflect general disease notifications, not exclusively Hepatitis A; verify exact indicator definition.' This is a fundamental substitution of an unvalidated indicator for a specific epidemiological measure.", "CRITICAL: Data source not authentic. Hypothesis cites CDC/WHO Notifiable Diseases Surveillance System (NDSS) at https://www.cdc.gov/diseases-conditions/hepatitis-a/. Script acknowledged this 'provides PDFs only, not machine-readable data' but then used an undocumented WHO GHO indicator (WHS3_41) instead without clear justification that WHS3_41 is from NDSS or equivalent.", "MAJOR: Severe correlation-hypothesis mismatch. Expected r\u22480.55\u20130.70; observed Pearson r=0.072 (p&lt;0.0001). This is a ~10-fold gap. Spearman rho=0.201 is similarly far below hypothesis expectation.", "MAJOR: Outlier/masking concern. With 5046 observations across 196 countries and such a weak overall correlation despite statistically significant p-values, there are likely large country-level heterogeneities or ceiling/floor effects (e.g., universal vaccination in high-HDI countries masking the HAV-WASH signal). No outlier analysis or stratification by HDI/vaccination coverage was performed.", "MODERATE: Partial correlation not computed. Script attempted to aggregate to country-level means but 'partial = None' in final output. Without GDP/capita control, cannot assess whether the weak correlation is confounded by development level.", "MODERATE: Functional form untested. Script attempted test_functional_form() but 'functional_form = None' in final result. Hypothesis specifies nonlinear relationship; no evidence presented that linear form is adequate.", "MINOR: Year alignment appears sound (merged on iso+year, 5046 rows from 196 countries suggests reasonable temporal coverage), but given the weak correlation, temporal misalignment of proxy to target cannot be ruled out as a contributing factor."]</data>
    </edge>
