    <edge source="proxy:WRR-H01" target="indicator:WRR">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">WRR-H01</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">log-linear</data>
      <data key="d28">mechanistically clear correlation</data>
      <data key="d29">Composting capacity sets ceiling on possible recovery rates—no country can recover more waste than its infrastructure allows. Between 2013 and 2023, approximately 40 new facilities began operations, coinciding with expansion of state organics waste bans and municipal composting mandates.</data>
      <data key="d30">partially_confirmed</data>
      <data key="d31" />
      <data key="d32" />
      <data key="d33" />
      <data key="d34" />
      <data key="d35" />
      <data key="d36" />
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">[]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:WRR-H01" target="source:biocycle_magazine">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:WRR-H02" target="indicator:WRR">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">WRR-H02</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">linear</data>
      <data key="d28">direct mechanistic link</data>
      <data key="d29">Each WtE facility that operates diverts mass from landfill. In Denmark, Switzerland, and Belgium, incineration with energy recovery accounts for 50-70% of waste treatment, mechanistically driving elevated WRR. EPA reports 75 operational facilities process ~14% of municipal solid waste in the US.</data>
      <data key="d30">partially_confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">0.36179447384613106</data>
      <data key="d40">7.774661647301067e-06</data>
      <data key="d41">0.29442564686382944</data>
      <data key="d42">145</data>
      <data key="d35" />
      <data key="d36">linear</data>
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["CRITICAL: Hypothesis specified 'Waste-to-Energy plant capacity' (count/MW) but agent substituted 'People using basic hygiene services (SH.STA.HYGN.ZS)' \u2014 a fundamentally different variable measuring sanitation access, NOT waste infrastructure or WtE capacity. This is not a reasonable proxy but a conceptually unrelated variable.", "CRITICAL: Data source mismatch \u2014 hypothesis requires Statista WtE capacity data; agent used World Bank sanitation indicator instead. Substitution was documented in data_quality_notes but the variables measure entirely different constructs.", "The agent states 'sanitation access is a correlated but indirect proxy' but provides no empirical or theoretical justification for why basic hygiene services should correlate with WtE capacity. This is speculative.", "The positive correlation found (Pearson r=0.362, p&lt;0.0001) likely reflects broad economic/development patterns (wealthier countries have better both hygiene services AND waste infrastructure) rather than a mechanistic link between WtE capacity and WRR.", "No attempt was made to find alternative waste-management-specific indicators (e.g., Eurostat WtE data, national waste authority statistics, or OECD waste databases) before accepting a sanitation proxy.", "The verdict 'partially_confirmed' is misleading because the statistical test used a misaligned proxy variable, not the actual proxy specified in the hypothesis."]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:WRR-H02" target="source:statista">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:WRR-H03" target="indicator:WRR">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">WRR-H03</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">nonlinear</data>
      <data key="d28">strong documented correlation</data>
      <data key="d29">DRS raises economic value of containers from zero to deposit amount, making recovery economically rational. In New York, 57.5% redeem deposits with 14.6% donating, achieving 72% return rate. Germany achieves &gt;95% return rates for glass bottles.</data>
      <data key="d30">partially_confirmed</data>
      <data key="d31" />
      <data key="d32" />
      <data key="d33" />
      <data key="d34" />
      <data key="d35" />
      <data key="d36" />
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["MAJOR: Hypothesis specifies 'Deposit return scheme participation rates' as the proxy, but the script attempted to substitute World Bank recycling rate indicators (EN.MSW.RCYC.ZS, EN.MSW.INCN.ZS, EN.MSW.TOTL.PC.KG) instead. These are materially different variables\u2014recycling rates are aggregate outcomes, not DRS participation measures. This is a substantial conceptual deviation from the hypothesis.", "MAJOR: The Reloop Platform PDF source specified in the hypothesis could not be machine-parsed, and the script fell back to a literature-only verdict without acquiring the actual proxy data from the stated source. The data_source_authentic check flags this: no country-level DRS participation panel data was obtained from Reloop or any alternative structured source.", "MAJOR: Final result contains n_observations=null and n_countries=null with no statistical test performed. The verdict is 'partially_confirmed' based on literature alone, which means the country_coverage_adequate criterion cannot be evaluated. The merged dataset was reported as having insufficient data (&lt; 20 rows), failing the minimum threshold.", "The script's fallback to literature-only verdict is reasonable given data unavailability, but this represents a significant gap between the hypothesis's proxy specification and what was actually tested.", "Data quality notes acknowledge the substitution and the absence of structured DRS participation data, which is transparent but does not resolve the fundamental mismatch between hypothesis proxy (DRS participation rates) and tested proxy (general recycling rates)."]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:WRR-H03" target="source:reloop_platform">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:WRR-H04" target="indicator:WRR">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">WRR-H04</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">threshold</data>
      <data key="d28">5-15 percentage point increase</data>
      <data key="d29">EPR creates financial responsibility for end-of-life management, incentivizing producers to use recyclable materials and funding collection/sorting infrastructure. Italy's Ronchi Decree raised separate collection from 9% in 1997 to 66.6% in 2023.</data>
      <data key="d30">confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">0.7177045412585347</data>
      <data key="d40">2.1782256950820875e-46</data>
      <data key="d41">0.7350149851678833</data>
      <data key="d42">285</data>
      <data key="d35" />
      <data key="d36">quadratic</data>
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["Critical: EPR implementation dates were manually compiled from literature/government sources rather than fetched from the PSI database or another machine-readable authenticated source. The script hardcodes ~80 country-year pairs as 'verifiable dates from official government records,' but this is a manual dataset construction, not data retrieval. While the dates may be accurate, this is a form of semi-synthetic data assembly that circumvents the original data source specification.", "The PSI database (epr.sustainablepackaging.org) is cited as the primary source in the hypothesis but was not actually used; the data_quality_notes acknowledge it is 'not machine-readable.' Instead, a substitute dataset was constructed. Although documented in data_quality_notes, this is a material deviation from the specified data source.", "Partial correlation controlling for confounders (e.g., GDP per capita) was not computed, even though the hypothesis explicitly cites 'Confounding with other waste legislation' and 'Confounding with other waste legislation' as caveats. The script attempted to load GPC but the null result suggests the merge failed or had insufficient observations; this limitation should have been investigated further.", "The functional form analysis shows a quadratic fit (R\u00b2=0.571) performs better than linear (R\u00b2=0.515), but the hypothesis specifies a 'threshold' functional form. A quadratic relationship does not match the claimed threshold mechanism, suggesting either the mechanism description is inaccurate or the data does not support the stated functional form.", "Implementation delays (1-3 years) and enforcement variability noted in caveats are not modeled in the proxy. EPR maturity is measured as years since legislation, but enforcement lags and heterogeneous design are not captured."]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:WRR-H04" target="source:product_stewardship_institute">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
