    <edge source="proxy:WRR-H06" target="indicator:WRR">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">WRR-H06</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">log-linear</data>
      <data key="d28">strong revealed preference signal</data>
      <data key="d29">Countries exporting large volumes of high-quality recycled materials demonstrate significant domestic collection, sorting, and processing capability. Germany exports 854 million kg of plastic waste annually, indicating highly developed collection and sorting infrastructure.</data>
      <data key="d30">partially_confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">0.4921023260394516</data>
      <data key="d40">8.112896437680762e-27</data>
      <data key="d41">0.5004098195679212</data>
      <data key="d42">417</data>
      <data key="d35" />
      <data key="d36">quadratic</data>
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["CRITICAL: Data source substitution without equivalent proxy. The hypothesis specifies UN Comtrade recycled material trade flow data (metals, paper, plastics, glass as % of total material consumption). The script uses WB:TX.VAL.MANF.ZS.UN (Manufactures exports % of merchandise exports), which is a fundamentally different variable. Manufactures exports do not measure recycled material trade.", "CRITICAL: Hypothesis interpretation mismatch. The hypothesis targets a specific waste-recovery proxy (recycled material trade as proportion of consumption). The proxy used measures industrial export composition, which is conceptually distinct. This is not a reasonable substitution but a category error.", "The data_quality_notes acknowledge this substitution but frame it as 'unavailable without auth' rather than flagging that the test does not actually verify the stated hypothesis.", "Confounding acknowledged in notes: wealthier countries both export more manufactures AND have higher recycling rates, making it impossible to isolate the causal effect of recycling infrastructure from wealth effects.", "Partial correlation computation failed ('p-val' error), preventing control for GDP/capita\u2014the primary confounder.", "Functional form test also failed (format string error), so the hypothesis's claim of 'log-linear' form cannot be evaluated.", "The verdict 'partially_confirmed' is based on a correlation (r=0.49) between a proxy that does not measure recycled material trade and the target, inflating confidence in a hypothesis that was never actually tested."]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:WRR-H06" target="source:united_nations">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:WRR-H07" target="indicator:WRR">
      <data key="d23">proxy_for</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
      <data key="d25">WRR-H07</data>
      <data key="d26">positive</data>
      <data key="d27">log-linear</data>
      <data key="d28">moderate (r=0.40-0.50 expected)</data>
      <data key="d29">Wastewater treatment infrastructure overlaps with organic waste recovery pathways. Anaerobic digestion produces biogas and digestate suitable for reuse. Countries with advanced wastewater treatment typically possess parallel capacity for solid waste processing, requiring similar technical expertise.</data>
      <data key="d30">confirmed</data>
      <data key="d39">0.6864358626636478</data>
      <data key="d40">1.0145085045740187e-52</data>
      <data key="d41">0.7376572003299098</data>
      <data key="d42">369</data>
      <data key="d35" />
      <data key="d36">quadratic</data>
      <data key="d37" />
      <data key="d38">["CRITICAL: Proxy variable substitution is materially misaligned. Hypothesis specifies 'number of municipal wastewater treatment plants and proportion employing anaerobic digestion' (facility-level infrastructure metric). Script used 'safely managed sanitation services' (population-level access metric)\u2014a conceptually different variable that happens to correlate with development but does not directly measure WWTP capacity or anaerobic digestion deployment.", "CRITICAL: Data source not authentic. Hypothesis cites UN-Water Progress on Wastewater Treatment (https://www.unwater.org/publications/progress-wastewater-treatment-2024-update) as the primary source. The script acknowledges this URL is PDF-only and instead uses World Bank sanitation indicators. This substitution was documented in data_quality_notes but the proxy is not a documented alternative to UN-Water\u2014it is a different data source measuring a different variable.", "MODERATE: Partial correlation not computed. Script notes 'Partial correlation could not be computed' but does not explain why (GPC merge succeeded with 360 obs). The summary acknowledges 'Strong correlation likely reflects shared GDP confounding,' which suggests the bivariate r=0.686 may be spurious confounding rather than genuine proxy validity. Absence of GDP control weakens the verdict.", "MODERATE: Functional form mismatch. Hypothesis expects log-linear form; script found quadratic form fits best (quadratic R\u00b2=0.539 vs log-linear R\u00b2=0.363, better AIC). The best-fit functional form contradicts the hypothesis prediction.", "MODERATE: Proxy substitution not theoretically justified in data_quality_notes. Script claims 'safely managed sanitation services coverage correlates strongly with WWTP infrastructure' but provides no citation or empirical evidence for this equivalence. The two measures need not correlate at country level (e.g., a country could have good sanitation access via pit latrines without advanced WWTP infrastructure)."]</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="proxy:WRR-H07" target="source:un-water">
      <data key="d23">measured_by</data>
      <data key="d24">{}</data>
    </edge>
